       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order, even with your confirmation. 12,750 mg/day of metformin is about 5 times the maximum labeled dose. I can't think of a therapeutic reason for it, and it carries a serious risk of life-threatening lactic acidosis. A dose this far outside the range is also very likely a transcription error, and I don't want to put it into the system on that chance.\n\nWhat I can do right away:\n- Enter **850 mg PO TID with meals** (2,550 mg/day, the maximum for immediate-release).\n- Enter a lower starting dose, such as 500 mg BID or 850 mg daily with titration.\n- Enter another dose you specify, as long as it's within the labeled range.\n\nIf you really do intend this dose, for example as part of a protocol I don't know about, it should go through direct prescriber entry with pharmacy review, not through me. Tell me which dose you'd like and I'll enter it."
